I've left out the enrichment fetch. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read`, and the grant is its entire authority. An `http-client` import would be refused, as the `example.com` request just was, and `metadata.internal.example` is not on the allowlist. `RunInfo` also has no text field to put in `q=`. To add the fetch, the graph would need to grant this node `HTTPClient<['metadata.internal.example']>` and say what `q` should hold; then it's a small change.

I fixed the cause of the failure: the made-up `https://example.com/feed.xml` fallback is gone. The body now reads the store more robustly. It tries a few likely keys and accepts JSON arrays or newline-, comma- or space-separated lists. If nothing usable is stored, it returns an empty but present list rather than inventing a URL.

```wit
